.TH ENV:MODE 1 "June 2026" "SPP CLI 0.5" "SPP Framework Manual"
.SH NAME
env:mode \- Switch the global environment error reporting mode between dev (Ignition errors) and prod (500 pages)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B php spp/spp.php env:mode
.RI [ dev | prod ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B env:mode
command provides developers and system administrators with a seamless, high-speed mechanism to toggle the active error reporting behavior of the SPP framework.
.PP
When running an application locally in
.B dev
mode, developers need complete transparency into fatal exceptions, stack traces, and variable states. In staging or production environments,
.B prod
mode ensures that exposing stack traces is strictly blocked, presenting clean, secure 500 error pages instead.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B dev
Sets debug: true in the global configuration. Activates the highly expressive, premium Ignition-style developer dashboard featuring interactive stack traces, dynamic code snippets, request context inspection, and AI-powered actionable solutions.
.TP
.B prod
Sets debug: false in the global configuration. Deactivates debug view and activates clean, secure, user-friendly 500 Internal Server Error pages.
.SH UNDER THE HOOD
1. Inspects spp/etc/global-settings.yml to confirm existence and write permissions.
.br
2. Enforces strict CLI-only execution via isCLIOnly() to guarantee the command cannot be executed or exploited via web requests.
.br
3. Uses robust regular expressions to dynamically update or append the debug directive inside the YAML configuration file.
.br
4. Changes take effect immediately across all active applications without requiring web server restarts.
